From: Jakub Zelenka <bukka@php.net>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:19:04 +0100
Subject: Fix GHSA-qc49-hpvq-g2w6: Drain unread request bodies

Opening php://input can create a request body stream without
consuming the input from the SAPI. Request shutdown treated the
stream as proof that the body was read and skipped the drain.

Drain whenever post_read is false, independently of whether the
stream exists. This keeps unread FastCGI STDIN bytes from being
parsed as another request when FCGI_KEEP_CONN is set.

As a final safeguard, reject a new FastCGI request if the
previous STDIN record was only partially consumed.

(cherry picked from commit 28014fd092c7acdafb9c074e735f099893a5ef66)
(cherry picked from commit 130836964c5c26b2421891a706ebad5f0b14f713)
(cherry picked from commit 51ec3171910cc4c9aa81bd96cadee1d99feb98f5)
(cherry picked from commit a539b19cdc1c7d807dc0774a3168dcd20107ac13)
(cherry picked from commit df339d81fcb940035252b1dd88fb6866c2bc179d)
(cherry picked from commit aecf2444ca6ffd6c223726d16d0facfe8941fc6b)
(cherry picked from commit e49ead238a7d95246bc5af24d410747e7301d413)
(cherry picked from commit a539653a74da633fec0ab4d90dab76388a8a6bf6)

adapt for 5.6: the FastCGI code lives in sapi/cgi and sapi/fpm there, the
test needs the FPM tester and is not included

debian-php-backports: ported to PHP 5.4.45 (php5 5.4.45-0+deb7u30): only the
FastCGI safeguard in sapi/cgi/fastcgi.c and sapi/fpm/fpm/fastcgi.c is ported
(unchanged). The main/SAPI.c hunk is dropped: 5.4 has no lazy request_body
stream (that came with 5.6.0). Its sapi_deactivate() either has the whole
body in post_data or reads the rest with sapi_module.read_post(), so the
unread body bug itself does not exist in 5.4.
---
 sapi/cgi/fastcgi.c     | 6 ++++++
 sapi/fpm/fpm/fastcgi.c | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sapi/cgi/fastcgi.c b/sapi/cgi/fastcgi.c
index 53e3202d..07b1e08b 100644
--- a/sapi/cgi/fastcgi.c
+++ b/sapi/cgi/fastcgi.c
@@ -885,6 +885,10 @@ static int fcgi_read_request(fcgi_request *req)
 	int len, padding;
 	unsigned char buf[FCGI_MAX_LENGTH+8];
 
+	if (UNEXPECTED(req->in_len != 0)) {
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	req->keep = 0;
 	req->closed = 0;
 	req->in_len = 0;
@@ -1138,6 +1142,8 @@ static inline void fcgi_close(fcgi_request *req, int force, int destroy)
 		req->nodelay = 0;
 #endif
 		req->fd = -1;
+		/* a partially read STDIN record does not outlive its connection */
+		req->in_len = 0;
 	}
 }
 
diff --git a/sapi/fpm/fpm/fastcgi.c b/sapi/fpm/fpm/fastcgi.c
index 80745a9c..26822f1b 100644
--- a/sapi/fpm/fpm/fastcgi.c
+++ b/sapi/fpm/fpm/fastcgi.c
@@ -503,6 +503,10 @@ static int fcgi_read_request(fcgi_request *req)
 	int len, padding;
 	unsigned char buf[FCGI_MAX_LENGTH+8];
 
+	if (UNEXPECTED(req->in_len != 0)) {
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	req->keep = 0;
 	req->closed = 0;
 	req->in_len = 0;
@@ -755,6 +759,8 @@ void fcgi_close(fcgi_request *req, int force, int destroy)
 		close(req->fd);
 #endif
 		req->fd = -1;
+		/* a partially read STDIN record does not outlive its connection */
+		req->in_len = 0;
 		fpm_request_finished();
 	}
 }
